1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[Turtle Ant] May we have your permission
to have names?

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[Queen] And what is a name?

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
[Turtle Ant] It's like a label, my queen,

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
one that can be used to identify
each of us individually.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
[Queen] Names, amusing little things.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
The three elite Royal Guards.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
I shall come up
with a name for you myself.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
[opening theme music playing]

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
[singer singing in English]

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[singer singing in English]

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
NO X GOOD X NGL

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[narrator] On the hunt
for the giant Chimera Ant,

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Kite's group has finally arrived
in the Mitene Union.

19
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Now they must travel
from the Rokario Republic

20
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
to the neighboring NGL Autonomous Region.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
You heading to the NGL, huh?

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
You know, they believe that the best way
to live is as naturally as possible.

23
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
They're pretty weird for living out there,

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
but you folks are even weirder
for wanting to visit them.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I don't have a clue what's going on there,

26
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
but I've already driven in
about ten big groups

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
just like you guys today alone.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Did you say ten?

29
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
[driver] That's right.

30
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
So if most of the other groups
are already arriving,

31
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
then we're among the last.

32
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
I'd guess they're other Pro Hunters.

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
You think they're all looking
for the giant insects?

34
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Yeah. Those seasoned veterans
are really something.

35
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
That must have been hard information
for them to get.

36
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
[Ponzu] Bugs large enough
to attack humans.

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Do you think they actually exist?

38
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Well, it's pretty unbelievable, I know,

39
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
but when you stop to consider the voice
they heard over the transmitter

40
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,000
and what it said…

41
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
[reporter] Monsters! Gigantic bugs!

42
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[static crackles]

43
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
It's possible it could be
some other kind of animal.

44
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
The NGL is one big nature preserve,

45
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
so it's said to be inhabited
by many organisms

46
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
that have yet to be discovered
by scientists.

47
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
It wouldn't be that strange if there were
insects that could attack humans.

48
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Even if there aren't any giant bugs,

49
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:51,000
if we can confirm the existence
of something new, it'll all be worth it.

50
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,000
As a new Magical-Beast Hunter myself,
it's important that I produce results.

51
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Now that I'm here,
I have to accomplish something.

52
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
[Peggy] According to the reports
from scouts

53
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
that went out on reconnaissance
first thing this morning,

54
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
there's a new human village
that has been discovered in Sector MA-18,

55
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
which is a region in the southwest.

56
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
There are 12 houses,

57
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,000
as well as an estimated
20 to 60 residents there.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Wow. That's pretty big, isn't it?

59
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Guess there are still
a few large villages left.

60
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I was under the distinct impression
we'd already cleaned out that area.

61
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
I shall add this one to the list.

62
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
It will be among our main targets today.

63
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Now, Colt, can you make the trip?

64
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Yes, of course.

65
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Hey, Peggy, why aren't you sending me out?

66
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Because I need you to go to the northwest
as we had originally planned, Cheetu.

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Zazan, you accompany him.

68
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,000
But I just don't believe there are
any large villages left in the northwest.

69
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
And if there are, I bet there aren't
any strong, young humans there.

70
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
It's a lot more fun for me
when I get to chase them around!

71
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Cheetu! We do not hunt for fun.

72
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
We are in service to the Queen.

73
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
We need only capture
the requested number of humans,

74
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
no more and no less.

75
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Yeah, yeah, I know that already.

76
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
We'll get the job done right, Colt.

77
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Right, Zazan?

78
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
I promise to fulfill the quota,

79
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
but I don't appreciate
you telling me how to hunt my prey.

80
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
I'll continue to do things as I please.

81
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Cheetu's right.
It's fun to hunt humans as they run.

82
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
What did you say?

83
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
I guess that's all there is to it.

84
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Let's go, Zazan.

85
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Don't get too worked up, Colt.

86
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Learn to relax every once in a while.

87
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Makes things a whole lot easier.

88
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Such insubordination.

89
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Their squad is going to fall apart
at this rate.

90
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Using names may be convenient,

91
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
at least when it comes to
leading the troops in battle,

92
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
but too much individuality
might become a serious issue.

93
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,000
It must be stopped
before it breaks down our command.

94
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
We simply can't allow this.

95
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Yes, I agree.
It's important something be done.

96
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
You'll notice that Meleoron and Yunju

97
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
have yet to show themselves
at a single war council.

98
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Hear that? Show yourself, Meleoron.

99
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Okay, but I just want to be clear
that it isn't my fault Yunju is absent.

100
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
[Peggy] Were you hiding because
you thought you would be blamed?

101
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
You are supposed to be
a squadron leader, correct?

102
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Now where is Yunju? Why isn't he here?

103
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:57,000
You see? It's me getting yelled at.
That's why I was hiding out.

104
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Everything here is always my fault, right?

105
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Well, hiding the truth
makes you complicit.

106
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
-and furthermore--
-Fine! I'll talk!

107
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
I mean, it's not like
I wanted to cover for him or anything.

108
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:12,000
He's the one who ran off
to hunt the humans by himself.

109
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
He what? In what sector?

110
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Has a new human village been discovered?

111
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
That's not it.

112
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You remember the humans, don't you,

113
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
the ones who fought back,
the ones who were armed with guns?

114
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[both gasp]

115
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
[Meleoron] Yunju was
really worked up about it.

116
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
He said he was gonna go
and make them his pets.

117
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[machine guns firing]

118
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
[panting]

119
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[man screams in distance]

120
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[screams]

121
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
[grunts]

122
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[groaning]

123
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Ah, come on.

124
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
You gotta keep moving,
or you might just get trampled.

125
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Is that all you've got?

126
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Come on. Entertain us more.

127
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
That's right. That's right!

128
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
[both laugh]

129
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Yunju] Run as if your lives depend on it!

130
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Until you're dead.

131
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
[slurps]

132
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,000
[chuckles]

133
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Well, this is it, guys,
the border of the NGL.

134
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Those two giant trees right there

135
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
serve as both
the checkpoint and the embassy.

136
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,000
[sighs] Kinda makes you wonder
what's out here in the middle of nowhere.

137
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Ah, well.
Some people are just weird, I guess.

138
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Prepare yourselves, everyone.

139
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:47,000
The Ants are a concern, but the NGL isn't
the ecofriendly group it claims to be.

140
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[Gon] Got it.

141
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
May I ask what brings you here?

142
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
[Kite] We're on a hunt.

143
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,000
A biohazard-class insect
might have infiltrated your country.

144
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Hmm.

145
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Well, if you're professional hunters,

146
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:12,000
I'm certain you're aware that
we cannot deny you entry into our land.

147
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Right this way.

148
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
[Killua] Wait. You're using
computers and machines here?

149
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:34,000
[man 1] We are not technically
within the bounds of the NGL proper yet.

150
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:38,000
This area is used for diplomacy
and trading information.

151
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
I see.
Are there similar facilities within?

152
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
No, sir, not a single one.

153
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:50,000
No machines of any kind
are allowed inside the borders of the NGL.

154
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Of course, visitors aren't allowed
to bring technology in with them either.

155
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
We're very strict about that kind of thing

156
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
which means you must remove metals,
petroleum derived materials, and the like,

157
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
anything of that nature on your person
before you can enter.

158
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Do you mean, like, my glasses?

159
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:13,000
That's right. If your clothes,
belts, shoes, even your underwear

160
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:17,000
contain any plastic, chemicals, or metal,
you must remove them.

161
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
That isn't funny.

162
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
You want us to strip naked?

163
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:27,000
That's not necessary. All-natural clothing
is available for purchase just upstairs.

164
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,000
And if there are any implants
inside your body,

165
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
dental implants, for example,
made of gold, silver,

166
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
or even silicon prosthetics
that cannot be removed,

167
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:42,000
I'm sorry to say,
but you won't be allowed to enter.

168
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
You understand.

169
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
SHOP

170
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Only the five of us are left?

171
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,000
I want you all to stand by
in the closest town.

172
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,000
We'll return here
within two weeks and contact you.

173
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
[Spinner] Roger that.

174
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
[woman] The inspection area is over there.

175
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Of course, there's a physical exam,
as well as an interview.

176
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Then, once those are completed,

177
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:20,000
there will also be X-rays,
ultrasound, and metal scans.

178
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Security's rather tight.

179
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
It is,

180
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:32,000
because people have smuggled guns in
by hiding the parts inside their bodies.

181
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:36,000
We often find cameras or cell phones
in people's rectums.

182
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Some have even trained animals
to carry laptops across the border

183
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
once they themselves were inside.

184
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Well, it looks like all of you are clean.

185
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Thank you all for your patience.
You may enter now, and Godspeed.

186
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[man 2] Welcome to the NGL.

187
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
[wind blowing]

188
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,000
All right. Now the hunt begins.

189
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
[horses neighing]

190
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[horses galloping]

191
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
HORSE RENTAL
12000J PER DAY

192
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
[man 1] Any sightings of giant insects?

193
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
I haven't heard of anything like that.

194
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
And even if there were any such creatures,

195
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
I doubt the citizens of this country
would make much of a fuss.

196
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
If any of us are killed
or attacked by animals,

197
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:53,000
we simply accept it
as nature taking its course, nothing more.

198
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[horses galloping]

199
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[Gon] Anyway, I think
we should follow along the coastline

200
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
and check out all the villages.

201
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,000
If we search them
and nothing unusual turns up,

202
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
then it's probably
not even in this country.

203
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Yeah, maybe,

204
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
but that's assuming that those guys
were telling us the truth back there.

205
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Gon] They're still following us,
aren't they?

206
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
[Killua] Yeah.

207
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
[Killua] They say they're here
in case we meet unknown tribes

208
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
and need interpreters or intermediaries,

209
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
But they're obviously spies.

210
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Well, I never expected
the people here to be of any help.

211
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
But my instincts are saying

212
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
it's here somewhere.

213
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[footsteps approaching]

214
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[panting]

215
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[groans]

216
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Don't move a muscle.

217
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
If you die, you can't blame me for it.

218
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
You… You're just a mere animal.

219
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:08,000
You shouldn't be bossing
a superior human around.

220
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
[Koala Ant] "Mere animal"?

221
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
I don't understand.

222
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Why don't you explain
how you and I are different?

223
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Shut up!

224
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,000
[sighs]

225
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Good grief.

226
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
You should answer
when someone asks you something.

227
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Or didn't your parents
ever teach you that?

228
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
[gasping]

229
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
You are hopeless, old man.

230
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
[splashing]

231
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
You can try again in your next life.

232
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[Meleoron] Aw, man!

233
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,000
You killed him.

234
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
How are we supposed to keep him fresh
if you kill him?

235
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:08,000
[sighs] I can just make up
a batch of meatballs.

236
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
I'll serve them to her within the day.

237
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Humans like that one irritate me.

238
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
They should be put in their place.

239
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
I much prefer to see them running,
terrified for their lives.

240
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Heh. Yesterday, you shot a kid in the back
while he ran away screaming, didn't you?

241
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
If you let me handle this,
I could have secured our prey

242
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
in a much smarter fashion than this,
I promise you.

243
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:40,000
When you said, "Don't move,"
that was meant for me, wasn't it?

244
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Giving your squad leader an order, huh?

245
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[spits]

246
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I wouldn't get too cocky if I were you.

247
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
You're lucky I'm such a nice guy,
so I'll let it slide this time.

248
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,000
If you enjoy killing so much,
you should volunteer as a feeder.

249
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
It's hopeless.

250
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
[wings fluttering]

251
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
[Colt] Damn that Yunju.

252
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
[child crying]

253
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,000
[Rammot] Shut up!

254
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Quit your whining,
or I'll eat you right here and now!

255
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
-[Colt] Rammot!
-Huh?

256
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
What are you doing there?

257
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
You can't tell? I'm transporting the food.

258
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Isn't it obvious?

259
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Then, be more selective.

260
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
I'm tired of telling you.

261
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
The one you have is worthless.

262
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Besides, we've already met our quota
for the day.

263
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
You're wasting your time.

264
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[Rammot groans] Then I'll eat it myself.

265
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[Colt] What?

266
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Well, it's going to be eaten
sooner or later.

267
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Put it down and walk away.

268
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
That's an order.

269
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
[snarls]

270
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
-[child crying]
-[Rammot] Hmph!

271
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Damn it all. So much insubordination.

272
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
What?

273
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
Is there a problem?

274
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
I enjoy what I do.

275
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
You want this one?

276
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
[sighs] I guess it's dead, so you can't.

277
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Which squadron are you from?

278
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
[Chimera Ant chitters]

279
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
-Huh?
-[Chimera Ant chitters]

280
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
I see. Zazan, huh?

281
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
She is a nasty one, isn't she?

282
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
My sympathies.

283
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
[Chimera Ant chitters]

284
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Well, you could join Yunju's team,
couldn't you?

285
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,000
I hear they're allowed to kill
as many humans as they want.

286
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
If you take this as a gift,

287
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
he'll let all of you join up
on the spot.

288
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
What in the hell is this?

289
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
It's terrible.

290
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
But who could have done this?

291
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,000
[gasps]

292
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
[Balda] A gun?

293
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Wait. People are fighting with guns?

294
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:38,000
[Balda] Who, and how?
Guns aren't allowed in the NGL.

295
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
[Pokkle] They're members
of the NGL underground

296
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
that manufactures DD.

297
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[others gasps]

298
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:49,000
From the look of it,
these wounds were not made by humans.

299
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Does that mean…

300
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
It's too soon to be sure just yet.

301
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
But if the monster we seek
was responsible,

302
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
we won't be able to handle it
with the members we have.

303
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
[brush rustling]

304
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[Pekuba] There they are! Monsters!

305
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[horses neighing]

306
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[Pokkle] Ponzu! Balda! Pekuba!

307
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Run away on my signal.

308
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
[Pokkle] Got it?

309
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Rainbow!

310
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Time for Red Arrow!

311
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
[wails]

312
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Now run!

313
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Huh?

314
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
[splash]

315
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Completely hopeless.

316
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
[panting]

317
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Huh?

318
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
[chittering]

319
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[Ponzu screams]

320
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[whimpering]

321
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Hey, over here!

322
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
-You okay?
-Yeah.

323
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Okay, then.
We need to contact the other Pro Hunters.

324
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Think you can handle that?

325
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[machine guns firing]

326
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
[gunfire in distance]

327
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,000
[gunfire stops]

328
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
[flesh squelching]

329
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[Yunju] What? Is that all there is?

330
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
[Centipede Ant] No. There are more.

331
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
[bullets rattle]

332
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Oh, my! There sure are!
I recognize the smell of living humans.

333
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[cackles]

334
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
[laughing]

335
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[sighs]

336
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
What now, Zaikahal?

337
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,000
[narrator] The Chimera Ants
continue their rampage

338
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
and have now cornered
this country's shadowy ruler.

339
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
A storm brews in the NGL,

340
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
and Gon's group,
utterly unaware of that fact,

341
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
is heading straight for its center.

342
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,000
[closing theme music playing]

343
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

344
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[upbeat music playing]

345
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
[Gon] Next time, Evil and Terrible.

346
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
-[moans]
-[Killua] What's wrong, Gon?

347
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,000
-You have a fever?
-[Gon moans]

348
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
-[Killua] What? You strained your back?
-[Gon] It's terrible.

349
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
